Q7. Q7. Explain the strengths and weaknesses of DES. What are Double DES and Triple DES?
It provides an avalanche effect, where a small change in input can change many output bits.
It was widely used for secure communication.
Weaknesses of DES:
Its effective key length is only 56 bits.
It can be broken using modern brute-force attacks.
Differential and linear cryptanalysis can be used to study weaknesses in its design.
Double DES: It applies DES encryption twice using two keys. However, it is vulnerable to a meet-in-the-middle attack, which reduces its expected security.
Triple DES (3DES): It applies DES three times. It was developed to improve security over DES. It can use two or three independent keys, but it is slow and has a small block size. AES is preferred for modern applications.
